Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "Nighttime Pedestrian Near Vehicle" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :BehaviorAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :actor1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2 .

:actor1 a :Pedestrian ;
    :description "Person walking near vehicle with hand extended" .

:weather1 a :NightCondition .

:risk1 a :PedestrianCollisionRisk ;
    :description "Pedestrian near vehicle with potential collision risk due to proximity and movement" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Potential occlusion of pedestrian by vehicle due to blind spot or limited visibility" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.90"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .
```

Identified Risks for each risk class:

**Risk 1:**
Description: Pedestrian near vehicle with potential collision risk due to proximity and movement.
Severity Score: 0.90

**Risk 2:**
Description: Potential occlusion of pedestrian by vehicle due to blind spot or limited visibility.
Severity Score: 0.75